§ `Group proceedings: the representative plaintiff's questions`

§§ `Bringing the group proceeding`

@export Can I bring a group proceeding (class action) in the Supreme Court of Victoria on behalf of others with claims against the same person (Supreme Court Act 1986 ss 33B, 33C, 33D, 33G)?
GIVEN `number of claimants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons, counting you, have claims against the same person
      `same circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all those claims are in respect of, or arise out of, the same, similar or related circumstances
      `common question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all those claims give rise to a substantial common question of law or fact
      `kind of proceeding` IS A `Kind of proceeding` @desc What the proceeding is: a claim of any other kind (most claims for injury, loss or money), or one of the kinds Part 4A excludes (a proceeding under sections 34 and 35, about a deceased estate, about trust property, or under Order 18)
      `cross-vesting only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court would have jurisdiction over every one of the claims only by cross-vesting (answer no if unsure)
      `I have a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are yourself one of the persons with a claim against that person
      `sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a sufficient interest to sue that person on your own behalf
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I bring a group proceeding for us all` MEANS
    `s 33D -- I may commence it as representative` (`s 33C -- a group proceeding may be commenced` `number of claimants` `same circumstances` `common question` `kind of proceeding` `cross-vesting only`) `I have a claim` `sufficient interest`

@export If my own claim against the defendant ends (for example I settle it), may I still continue the group proceeding and appeal from its judgment (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33D(2))?
GIVEN `I commenced it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person who commenced the group proceeding (answer no if you were later substituted as plaintiff)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I continue after my own claim ends` MEANS
    `s 33D(2) -- I keep standing after my own claim ends` `I commenced it`

§§ `Costs`

@export Who must pay the defendant's costs if the Court orders costs against our side: me, or our law practice under a group costs order (Supreme Court Act 1986 ss 33ZD(1)(a), 33ZDA(2))?
GIVEN `group costs order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has made a group costs order (legal costs as a percentage of what is recovered) in the proceeding
GIVETH A `Who answers for the defendant's costs`
`Who answers for the defendant's costs, as plaintiff` MEANS
    `s 33ZD, 33ZDA(2) -- who answers for the defendant's costs` `group costs order`

@export May the Court make a group costs order, so that our lawyers are paid a percentage of what is recovered, shared by me and all group members (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33ZDA(1))?
GIVEN `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, as plaintiff, have applied for a group costs order
      `Court satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied that the order is appropriate or necessary to ensure that justice is done in the proceeding
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May the Court make a group costs order on my application` MEANS
    `s 33ZDA(1) -- the Court may make a group costs order` `I have applied` `Court satisfied`

@export Under a group costs order, what are the total legal costs taken from the award or settlement (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33ZDA(1)(a), (3))?
GIVEN `group costs order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has made a group costs order in the proceeding
      `percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage set in the order (as amended, if it was), e.g. 25 for 25%
      `amount recovered` IS A NUMBER @desc The total amount of the award or settlement recovered in the proceeding, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What are the legal costs under the order, as plaintiff` MEANS
    `s 33ZDA(1)(a) -- the legal costs under the group costs order` `group costs order` `percentage` `amount recovered`

@export How much of my unrecovered costs can the Court order paid to me out of the damages awarded (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33ZJ)?
GIVEN `damages awarded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has made an award of damages in the group proceeding
      `Court satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court, on your application, is satisfied that your reasonably incurred costs are likely to exceed the costs you can recover from the defendant
      `costs incurred` IS A NUMBER @desc The costs you reasonably incurred in relation to the group proceeding, in dollars
      `costs recoverable` IS A NUMBER @desc The costs you can recover from the defendant, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my costs can come out of the damages` MEANS
    `s 33ZJ -- the most that may be paid out of the damages for the representative's costs` `damages awarded` `Court satisfied` `costs incurred` `costs recoverable`

§§ `Settling (only if a settlement is proposed)`

@export May the group proceeding be settled or discontinued (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33V)? Not without the Court's approval.
GIVEN `approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has approved the settlement or discontinuance
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I settle or discontinue the group proceeding` MEANS
    `s 33V -- the group proceeding may be settled or discontinued` `approved`

@export May I settle my own individual claim during the group proceeding (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33W(1))?
GIVEN `leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has given you leave to settle your individual claim (in whole or in part)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I settle my own claim` MEANS
    `s 33W(1) -- I may settle my individual claim` `leave`

@export Having settled my own claim, can the Court order that I stop being the plaintiff (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33W(2), (4))?
GIVEN `settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have settled your individual claim in whole or in part
      `notice given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied that notice of the application was given to group members under s 33X(1)
      `notice in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied that the notice was given in time for a group member to apply to be substituted as plaintiff
      `substitute ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied that an order substituting another group member as plaintiff has been or will be made
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I stop being the plaintiff` MEANS
    `s 33W(2), (4) -- I may be ordered to cease to be plaintiff` `settled` `notice given` `notice in time` `substitute ordered`

§§ `If the proceeding stops being a group proceeding (only after an order under s 33L, 33M or 33N)`

@export If the Court orders that the proceeding no longer continue as a group proceeding, may I continue it for my own claim (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33P(a))?
GIVEN `order made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has ordered under s 33L, 33M or 33N that the proceeding no longer continue under Part 4A
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I continue on my own claim` MEANS
    `s 33P(a) -- I may continue on my own behalf` `order made`
